<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kinross-shire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as County of Kinross</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kinross-shire is a historic county of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, one of the smallest in the country, centred on the town of Kinross and Loch Leven, where Mary, Queen of Scots was imprisoned in 1567–1568. Lying between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fife">Fife</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perthshire">Perthshire</a>, it is now part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perth">Perth</a> and Kinross council area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kinross-shire.jpg" alt="Kinross-shire" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Visitor from Wikishire. This particular view by User:Inops · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinross-shire-Scotland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
